  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-03-08T17:34:17.540Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "At the current time of posting this there are no places anywhere I can find that have a complete list of developers, staff, employees, or moderation staff for VRChat. There does exist a list of folks on the official VRChat Discord, though these roles (primarily the moderation ones) are specific to the Discord itself and not VRChat in-game. I find it both frustrating and unprofessional that nobody seems to know who is an actual moderator in-game except by word-of-mouth. In every other online multiplayer game I have ever played, there is a staff list, and clear visible indicators of moderation/staff status on players. I understand the need arises sometimes to be able to observe players without disruption or detection, but I have heard that in such cases they can make themselves undetectable and invisible. Being that the case I find it both good for transparency to the community, and useful for fellow players, to know who exactly has power over them in this game.",
